  partName: Left Rear Bolt
  description: The Left Rear Bolt is a tiny, complex-shaped component located at
    the bottom-left-center of the engine, made of Material.001, which plays a crucial
    role in securing the engine's rear section. Its small size belies its importance,
    as it helps maintain the engine's structural integrity. Interestingly, the Left
    Rear Bolt is designed to withstand high torque forces, ensuring the engine's
    reliability.
